 "contract": "shell-builtin-inventory-v1",
 "purpose": "Record the names each shell resolves as a builtin, so the frontend's table can be checked for completeness against a measurement rather than against memory.",
 "note": "A builtin never reaches the PATH lookup, so lowering one to an Exec substitutes a different program. The frontend's table therefore has to mention every name a shell reports \u2014 including the ones nobody has decided about, which is the difference between `surveyed and found nothing to model` and `nobody looked`. The treatment column is the frontend's answer for each name; `unexamined` delegates like `delegated` does and is kept apart from it so the list of what is left to do is a value rather than an absence.",
